course: dictionary
lesson: 2270
title: Creature
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A creature is any living animal, big or small, like a bird, insect or fish. «Old forests with big trees are home to many fungi and creatures.» Here the word creatures means the living animals that live in those forests.
explain: A creature can also be a made-up being in a story. «A Gryphon (also spelled griffin) is a creature from old stories, half eagle and half lion.» The words from old stories are the clue. A gryphon is not a real animal, so the author means a made-up creature.
explain: Use the words around creature to decide which kind it is. Ask yourself: is this creature alive in the real world, or is it in a story? «Whenever Alice asks a sensible question, the two creatures call her dull» tells you the creatures are characters in a story, not real animals.
fact: A creature is a living thing, usually an animal.
fact: «Creature» can mean a real animal, like a bird, insect or fish.
fact: «Creature» can also mean a made-up being in a story, like a dragon or a monster.
fact: Scientists talk about sea creatures and creatures of the rainforest when they study how animals survive.
fact: The phrase «creature of habit» describes someone who likes to do things the same way every day.
exercise: Which of these is a living creature, big or small? | A rock | *A bee | A pencil | A cup
exercise: «Old forests with big trees are home to many fungi and creatures.» What does creatures mean here? | *Living animals of the forest | Old, empty houses | Tall trees with thick trunks | Rainy weather
exercise: Which of these is a made-up creature from a story? | Salmon | Robin | Ant | *Dragon
test: «Much of the world's oil formed long ago from the remains of tiny sea creatures.» Were these sea creatures real or made up? | *Real living animals that lived long ago | Big rocks under the sea | Made-up beings from a story | Tall trees on the shore
test: In the book, Alice calls the two creatures dull. What kind of creatures are they? | Trees in a forest | *Made-up beings in a story | Sea fish in the ocean | Real birds in a park
exam: Which sentence uses creature to mean a made-up being? | A sea creature swam past the boat. | *The dragon was a fierce creature in the book. | The insect is a tiny creature in the garden. | Bees are busy creatures in summer.
